Notebook[{
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Quantum Waves in Motion: Numerical Modeling of the Time-Dependent Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger Equation",
 FontSize->48]], "Title"],
Cell["A numerical solution of the Time-Dependent Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger Equation using a finite-domain time-difference method", "Subtitle"],
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Written by Yoogeun Song. This mini-project was conducted from March 11 to April 1, 2025.",
 FontSize->24,
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle"],
Cell[" ", "Text",
 Editable->False,
 Selectable->False,
 CellFrame->{{0, 0}, {0, 2}},
 ShowCellBracket->False,
 CellMargins->{{0, 0}, {1, 1}},
 CellElementSpacings->{"CellMinHeight"->1},
 CellFrameMargins->0,
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
 CellSize->{Inherited, 4}],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["1. Introduction",
 FontSize->36,
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Chapter"],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Project Objective:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell["This notebook solves the time-dependent Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation (TDSE) numerically for an electron, using a finite-difference time-domain (FDTD) scheme on a closed spatial box. The aim is partly the numbers and partly the pictures: once the solver works, you can watch a wave packet disperse, bounce off walls and leak through barriers.", "Text",
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Theoretical Background:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell[TextData[{
 "The TDSE, ",
 StyleBox["i\[HBar] \[PartialD]\[CapitalPsi](x,t)/\[PartialD]t = H(x) \[CapitalPsi](x,t)",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", governs how a quantum state evolves. The Hamiltonian ",
 StyleBox["H(x)",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " has a kinetic part, ",
 StyleBox["-\[HBar]\:00b2/(2m) \[PartialD]\:00b2/\[PartialD]x\:00b2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and a potential part ",
 StyleBox["V(x)",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellDingbat->"\[FilledSmallCircle]",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 "Finite differences discretise both time (",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ") and space (",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "), turning the TDSE into an update rule that can be iterated."
}], "Text",
 CellDingbat->"\[FilledSmallCircle]",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 "The full derivation, including the split into real and imaginary update equations, is in the accompanying ",
 StyleBox["report.pdf",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Methodology:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell[TextData[{
 "The initial state is a ",
 StyleBox["normalised Gaussian wave packet",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", modulated by cosine and sine factors to give it momentum, sampled on a discrete spatial grid (1000 points across 500 nm by default)."
}], "Text",
 CellDingbat->"\[FilledSmallCircle]",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 "The wavefunction is split into its ",
 StyleBox["real",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["imaginary",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " components, each stepped forward with a finite-difference update. The split keeps the whole calculation in real arithmetic."
}], "Text",
 CellDingbat->"\[FilledSmallCircle]",
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Simulation Setup & Exploration:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook is colour-coded and walks through the essential steps as well as the parameters you can change. Four potential landscapes are built in:\n\t\[Bullet] Free Particle: ",
 StyleBox["V(x) = 0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\t\[Bullet] Finite Square Well\n\t\[Bullet] Quadratic (Harmonic) Well\n\t\[Bullet] Step Potential\nSwapping between them is a one-line change, which makes comparing their effect on the packet's evolution easy."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Visualisation & Analysis:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell[TextData[{
 "At each saved frame the simulation records the probability density ",
 StyleBox["|\[CapitalPsi](x,t)|\:00b2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and the frames become animations (as ",
 StyleBox["videos or GIFs",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ") showing dispersion, reflection, interference and tunnelling."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16],
Cell["The obvious next step is time-dependent potentials; the Runge\[Dash]Kutta machinery in Chapter 2 already accepts them.", "Text",
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Usage Instructions:",
 FontSize->24]], "Section"],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Overview: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The notebook first fixes the physical context and the potential landscape, then builds and displays the initial wavefunction, then runs the example simulations of Chapter 3. The later sections are meant to be edited: change the parameters and re-run."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Colour-Coded Cells:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Green cells",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["Essential steps that must be evaluated sequentially",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,
 Background->RGBColor[0.88, 1, 0.88]],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Orange cells:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Cells that allow user input for customisation."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,
 Background->RGBColor[1, 0.9, 0.8]],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Watch-face cells",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " mark the slower steps: the time-evolution runs, the plot generation and the animation exports. Thanks to the vectorised update in Chapter 2 they take seconds to a couple of minutes each."
}], "Text",
 CellDingbat->"\[WatchIcon]",
 FontSize->16,
 Background->RGBColor[0.94, 0.91, 0.88]],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Light magenta cells",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " are extra cells that are optional."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,
 Background->RGBColor[1, 0.9, 1]],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Execution Order: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "For best results, ",
 StyleBox["please evaluate all cells in the order provided",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16],
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Output: ",
